    "summary": "Turn 29, final minutes of the run (≈4 minutes of allocation). The draft was re-validated (valid=true) and is submitted unchanged, i.e. the same closing handoff already accepted last turn; I am not manufacturing new claims or rewording it, so a duplicate acceptance is the expected outcome. This run is complete from my side: one confirmed defect — claim CLM-DURABLE-BAL on direct artifact 87fc8f1efa2d45dbb73c2f97b1c7ae58, executed as CheckRun f298950cf3b549d781b884912385770a, reviewed under semantic review 18a7858ac95f499698982a28685c7dd1, assessment outcome=violated with confirmed=true, bounded_complete=true, reviewed_complete=true, correspondence=no_issue_found and no blockers, unit-CLM-DURABLE-BAL status checked. The defect: in a Durable replica with bal (7) differing from vbal (2), epaxos.Replica.recordInstanceMetadata writes a 21-byte per-instance metadata record whose first four bytes are 2 (vbal) with bal_persisted false, because its two PutUint32 calls target the same b[0:4] offset, so the instance ballot is never persisted; the durable format additionally carries no instance addressing and no per-instance command delimiting (recorded this run). Weaker results stay labelled as such: four candidates explained by sourced mechanisms (inert TryPreAccept defer-cycle guard behind the duplicated sub-case 3/4 predicate; unreachable handleCommit nil-lb branch because the row owner always creates its own row entries; missing Accept-reply escalation bounded by the executeCommands recovery timer; client positional reply pairing matching request order for the modelled single-closest-replica client) and two candidates paused with premises recorded (even-N quorum arithmetic narrowed to a restart-dependent precondition, and the durability candidate superseded by the confirmed check). Open frontier for a future run: whether the lost ballot has an operational consequence (needs a durable-record reader, none in the captured source), whether the durable format gaps